## Goal

A finalist whose line won on determinization 0 (the world the beam searched) and on none of the other scored worlds is ranked by its mean on those others. Today it gets the plain mean (about 333,000), which beats every real board play. These keep the plain mean:
- a win on world 0 plus another world;
- a one-world decision (`worldsScored` 1);
- every loss.

The lethal solver, the lethal hint and the concession check are untouched. The means become a pure `pub fn finalist_means`, switched by `AI_SEARCH.confirm_lone_win`: shipped `true`, and `false` gives today's means bit for bit. The win floor is a named constant. Ruling R4608000, §9.9, the README and the tests (unit tests and two `scenario()` tests) record and prove it.

